A||||1||MooCow||What to do before driving 700 miles on my car??||||5||
Z||000000||MooCow||10-16-2000||09:11 PM||||Okay well i am now going to see Ed Parks the first weekend in November to switch my 4-spped Fiero for an auto one.  I was going to haul mine down there with my little truck but instead I am thinking of jsut driving it.  Now what should I do before I drive it about 700 miles straight.  I already did the spark plugs and an oil change.  What else should be done before I go??  Should I bring some water and some antifreeze or extra belt or something??<P>                              Thanks Ken||||reg||5
Z||000001||Old Lar||10-16-2000||09:50 PM||||What has broken on the car?  Take some fuses, a cell phone, membership in AAA a good credit card. I always take a ratchet set, screwdivers, (torxx) and some wrenches.<P>If the car uses oil...a quart of oil.  But you'll be getting a couple of tanks of gas, so you could just check the oil and replace if necessary.<P>Belts if the belts are worn,  I've only replaced one belt on the road in 35 years + of driving.  I had a spare because I knew the belt was going.  It was a lot easier in them days to replace a belt. (When a timing belt broke, well that was a couple of days lost)<P>An air pump to inflate leaky tires if they leak. (Credit card to fix flats). Keep micro spare inflated 60psi.<P>If the car has been fairly reliable, you shouldn't have any problems.  Just don't go driving at 100 mph for the trip.  For a 700 mile trip, plan on 11 hours drive time and that may be pushing it. That's averaging over 60 mph.  You will have to stop for gas, food and relief.<P>Have a fun trip to Ed's place.<P>Twin Lakes Fiero is in Illinois and a lot closer to Michigan.<p>[This message has been edited by Old Lar (edited 10-16-2000).]||||reg||3
